# Caddy reverse proxy for the single-host Twenty deployment.
# Automatic HTTPS via Let's Encrypt (HTTP-01) — no certs to manage.
#
# Requirements for the cert to issue:
#   - DNS A record  {$DOMAIN}  ->  this VM's public IP
#   - Ports 80 and 443 reachable from the internet (Oracle security list + ufw)
#
# The server container serves BOTH the frontend and the API on :3000, so a
# single origin is all that's needed.

{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}
}

{$DOMAIN} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy server:3000
}

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MULTI-TENANT (workspace subdomains) — optional upgrade.
# Twenty puts each workspace on its own subdomain when IS_MULTIWORKSPACE_ENABLED
# is true, which needs a wildcard *.{$DOMAIN}. To enable it, REPLACE the block
# above with the following (and set IS_MULTIWORKSPACE_ENABLED=true in .env, plus
# add a `*.{$DOMAIN}` A record -> this VM):
#
# {
# 	email {$ACME_EMAIL}
# 	# Issues a cert per workspace subdomain on first request (no DNS API needed).
# 	on_demand_tls {
# 		ask http://server:3000/healthz
# 	}
# }
#
# {$DOMAIN} {
# 	encode zstd gzip
# 	reverse_proxy server:3000
# }
#
# *.{$DOMAIN} {
# 	encode zstd gzip
# 	reverse_proxy server:3000
# 	tls {
# 		on_demand
# 	}
# }
#
# For many workspaces, prefer a single wildcard cert via the DNS-01 challenge
# instead of on-demand — see ORACLE_FREE_DEPLOY.md > "Multi-tenant subdomains".
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
